    "body": "The existing Runs view now exposes exact coordinator state/generation, current readiness/fence, last update, original fault and saved recovery receipt. A current owner can explicitly recover a faulted/blocked coordinator using the exact generation and a stable tab-retained request key. After an unknown reply, the panel reads saved health without dispatching another mutation. New faults require a fresh explicit current-generation request once the old recovery is completed.\n\nThis draft targets main after the accepted PR101 merge and normal-composes the whole immutable/cold recovery-ack fixes. Both coordinator operations are exactly pinned. Closed catalog/actor/body-hash/generation/readiness validation, current owner controls, bounded tab storage, stale read/write/session/navigation fences, finite request deadlines and AbortController/listener cleanup preserve the existing server authority. Coordinator health is rendered independently even when the Run list read fails. It introduces no new health-poll timer, compute retry, grant or reservation.\n\nLocal production source38c7844: controlled controller checks and2 canonical-pin unittests passed; existing mocked image-recovery browser passed. Real PostgreSQL17/Chromium151 journey passed actual separate advisory-lock timeout/fault, keyboard owner recovery, deliberately dropped successful HTTP reply, saved-read reconciliation without another POST, one first neutral GO from the original queue, unchanged admission identity and1Run/1grant/1consumption, fresh reload/mouse refresh, and1440/390 layouts. Existing real neutral publication pause/reload/same-key resume/whole-hash download browser also passed. Both fixtures closed and dropped only their owned fresh schemas.\n\nExact source hashes, browser/domain receipts, screenshots and retained logs: `docs/plans/lab-workflow-reliability/reports/m2-coordinator-ui/validation.json`. Independent final source/test/docs review is clear. Hosted exact-head/post-merge qualification remains pending; full M2 acceptance is not yet closed. M3 timing is active separately. These are neutral process/UI witnesses with no CUDA, model-training or scientific acceptance claim.\n\nIndependent review identified and cleared a delivery-boundary correction at exact production source3c2b8d1: a new current-generation request that never reached the server can retry its exact saved body despite an older completed receipt; an incompatible incomplete receipt remains refused. The failing witness is retained and the corrected positive/negative controller cases passed. The real PostgreSQL/Chromium coordinator journey passed again at3c2b8d1; earlier publication/browser regression evidence remains attributed to38c7844.\n\nThe corrected head b4070b6 imports the real browser APIs and inert DOM methods needed by the controller test VM; product code and assertions are unchanged. Original hosted failure and local/independent whole-script red/green evidence are retained under reports/m2-coordinator-ui/ci-controller-fixture. Corrected-head hosted acceptance remains pending.\n\n\n<!-- browser-cleanup-qualification-20261020 -->\nLatest qualification head: `aa7115a4e148151d37f6895d053ae51b4b04ac2b`. This normal composition carries the reviewed fix for a publication-browser teardown race: await the existing bounded test-owned child shutdown helper before removing private Chromium profiles. Product code and functional assertions are unchanged relative to `b4070b60b0119c73284c4832610cc82ef471963a`. Root actual PostgreSQL/Chromium publication, coordinator, lineage, phase and scientific-reader browser checks passed at their affected owners; the scientific fixture remains synthetic terminal evidence. Required exact-head hosted CI is pending. PR102's earlier lifecycle failure is retained as a cleanup failure after publication assertions passed.\n",
